List all snapshots of an Organization.

USAGE:
  scw instance snapshot list [arg=value ...]

EXAMPLES:
  List all snapshots in the default zone
    scw instance snapshot list

  List all snapshots in fr-par-1 zone
    scw instance snapshot list zone=fr-par-1

ARGS:
  [page-token]             Token for pagination
  [page-size]              Number of snapshots to return per page
  [order-by]               Field to sort by (created_at_desc | created_at_asc | updated_at_desc | updated_at_asc)
  [project-id]             Project ID to use. If none is passed the default project ID will be used
  [snapshot-ids.{index}]   Filter by specific snapshot IDs
  [name]                   Filter by name
  [tags.{index}]           Filter by tags
  [base-volume-id]         Filter by base volume ID
  [zone=fr-par-1]          Zone to target. If none is passed will use default zone from the config (fr-par-1 | fr-par-2 | fr-par-3 | nl-ams-1 | nl-ams-2 | nl-ams-3 | pl-waw-1 | pl-waw-2 | pl-waw-3 | it-mil-1)

FLAGS:
  -h, --help                help for list
      --list-sub-commands   List all subcommands

GLOBAL FLAGS:
  -B, --beta             Enable beta mode
  -c, --config string    The path to the config file
  -D, --debug            Enable debug mode
  -H, --no-headers       Skip headers in human output
  -o, --output string    Output format: json or human, see 'scw help output' for more info (default "human")
  -p, --profile string   The config profile to use
      --web              open console page for the current resource
